### Step 1 — No Pipe: the id arrives as a string
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/raw/1

### Step 2 — Built-in ParseIntPipe: the id becomes a number
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/built-in/1

### Step 2 — Built-in ParseIntPipe with invalid input: returns 400
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/built-in/abc

### Step 4 — Custom ParsePositiveIntPipe: valid positive id
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/1

### Step 4 — Custom ParsePositiveIntPipe: negative id returns 400
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/-5

### Step 4 — Custom ParsePositiveIntPipe: zero returns 400
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/0

### Step 4 — Custom ParsePositiveIntPipe: non-number returns 400
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/abc

### Step 3 — Custom TrimStringPipe: spaces around the keyword are removed
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/search/   keyboard

### Step 3 — Custom TrimStringPipe: another search
GET http://localhost:3000/pipes/products/search/monitor
